#: src/reference/reference/sbt-dependency-tree.md:1
msgid "sbt dependencyTree"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-dependency-tree.md:4
msgid "Synopsis"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-dependency-tree.md:7
msgid ""
"`sbt` `dependencyTree` \\[_subcommand_\\] \\[_options_\\]<br> `sbt` "
"`dependencyTree` `list` \\[_options_\\]<br> `sbt` `dependencyTree` `graph` \\"
"[_options_\\]<br> `sbt` `dependencyTree` `html` \\[_options_\\]<br> `sbt` "
"`dependencyTree` `html-graph` \\[_options_\\]<br> `sbt` `dependencyTree` "
"`json` \\[_options_\\]<br> `sbt` `dependencyTree` `xml` \\[_options_\\]<br> "
"`sbt` `dependencyTree` `stats` \\[_options_\\]"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-dependency-tree.md:16
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-dependency-tree.md:19
msgid ""
"The `dependencyTree` task displays the dependency graph of your project in "
"various formats, helping you visualize and analyze transitive dependencies. "
"It is provided by the `DependencyTreePlugin`, which was in-sourced from "
"Johannes Rudolph's sbt-dependency-graph in sbt 1.4.0. The task resolves "
"dependencies before generating output, so it may trigger downloads if needed."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-dependency-tree.md:21
msgid "Usage"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-dependency-tree.md:23
msgid ""
"Run this in the sbt shell. The default subcommand is `tree`, which prints an "
"ASCII tree."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-dependency-tree.md:25
msgid "Subcommands"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-dependency-tree.md:27
msgid ""
"`tree` (default): Prints an ASCII tree of dependencies, showing hierarchical "
"relationships. Useful for quick overviews."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-dependency-tree.md:28
msgid ""
"`list`: Prints a flat list of all dependencies, one per line. Ideal for "
"scripting or grepping."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-dependency-tree.md:29
msgid ""
"`graph` / `dot`: Prints a GraphViz DOT file for visualization. The `dot` "
"alias is provided for compatibility."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-dependency-tree.md:30
msgid ""
"`html`: Creates a standalone HTML page with the dependency graph rendered as "
"text."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-dependency-tree.md:31
msgid ""
"`html-graph`: Creates an HTML page with an embedded GraphViz diagram "
"(requires GraphViz on the system)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-dependency-tree.md:32
msgid ""
"`json`: Prints dependencies in JSON format, structured for programmatic use."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-dependency-tree.md:33
msgid ""
"`xml`: Prints dependencies in GraphML format, suitable for graph analysis "
"tools."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-dependency-tree.md:34
msgid ""
"`stats`: Prints summary statistics, such as total dependencies and versions."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-dependency-tree.md:35
msgid ""
"`help`: Displays the usage help (same as running `dependencyTree` without "
"arguments)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-dependency-tree.md:37
msgid "Options"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-dependency-tree.md:39
msgid ""
"`--quiet`: Suppresses console output and returns the result as a task value "
"(e.g., for use in other tasks)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-dependency-tree.md:40
msgid ""
"`--out <file>`: Writes output to the specified file instead of stdout. The "
"file extension determines the default subcommand:"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-dependency-tree.md:41
msgid "`.txt`: `tree`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-dependency-tree.md:42
msgid "`.dot`: `graph`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-dependency-tree.md:43
msgid "`.html`: `html`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-dependency-tree.md:44
msgid "`.json`: `json`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-dependency-tree.md:45
msgid "`.xml`: `xml`"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-dependency-tree.md:46
msgid ""
"`--browse`: Automatically opens the output file in your default browser "
"(only works with `graph` or `html` subcommands)."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-dependency-tree.md:48
msgid "Examples"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-dependency-tree.md:50
msgid "ASCII Tree (Default)"
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-dependency-tree.md:52
msgid ""
"Displays a hierarchical view of dependencies, with `[S]` indicating Scala "
"library dependencies."
msgstr ""

#: src/reference/reference/sbt-dependency-tree.md:65
msgid ""
"Evicted dependencies (older versions replaced by newer ones) are shown in "
